-- title:
--   Ends of the supersingular component for q = 2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 2$, an integer $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, let $F_{ss}$ be a field over $\kappa$, and let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to the full-level field $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$) with reduction $F_{ss}$: thus $R$ consists of a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring homomorphism onto $F_{ss}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with the prescribed residue map, and such that every nonzero function becomes a unit after scaling. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $F_{ss}/\kappa$ (valuation subrings, proper, containing $\kappa$, principal). Assume: for all $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the pullback of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ is $R.\mathrm{integers}$; $\#N = q+1$; and $N$ is stable under $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by these level automorphisms that preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$. Assume further a $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, that the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa = \kappa[x,y]/(xy^q - x^qy - 1)$ is a domain, and fix $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, a subgroup $C_s \le \mu_{q+1}(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ and a $\kappa$-isomorphism $e$ from $F_{ss}$ onto $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$, the fixed field in $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the group generated by the actions of $(1,\zeta')$ for $\zeta' \in C_s$; assume $e$ intertwines the residual action of $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ with $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ of $(\gamma \bmod q, 1) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ for which these data are defined. Then: (1) a place $Q$ of $F_{ss}/\kappa$ satisfies $Q \notin N$ if and only if $e^{-1}(z) \in \mathcal O_Q$ for every $z$ in the fixed field whose image in $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ lies in the image of the coordinate ring; and (2) every place $Q \notin N$ is moved by some level automorphism: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma) \cdot Q \neq Q$.
--
--   This identifies the distinguished $(q+1)$-element set $N$ of places on a supersingular component of the semistable reduction with the places at infinity of the Drinfeld quotient curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ modulo $C_s$, the complement consisting exactly of the affine places, and records that no affine place is fixed by the whole level action. It is the $q = 2$ form, at an auxiliary rigidifying level divisible by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, of the corresponding statement for $q \ge 5$, and feeds the transitivity and mobility statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_levelAut_transitive_ends_moves_smoothPlaces_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_levelAut_transitive_ends_moves_smoothPlaces_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
